# Configuration for deploying TravelAgentWebStack (the hosted web UI on
# ECS Fargate behind a plain, non-authenticating ALB — the server itself
# runs the OIDC login flow against Okta; see DESIGN.md §2e, PLAN.md
# Phase 12). Optional: `cdk deploy`/`cdk synth` skip WebStack entirely if
# WEB_CERTIFICATE_ARN is unset, so you don't need this file at all if
# you're only running web/server.py locally for development.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values below. cdk/app.py loads it
# via a small dotenv-style reader (_load_dotenv()).
#
# Register a new, dedicated Okta OIDC web application (confidential
# client, with a client secret) for this purpose — do not reuse any other
# Okta app in your org for this. Configure it for the `openid
# offline_access` scopes and PKCE (S256), and configure it to keep
# issuing the *same*, non-rotating refresh token on every refresh (not
# Okta's rotate-on-use alternative) — this project's silent-refresh logic
# assumes a fixed refresh token. Register
# https://<WEB_HOSTNAME below>/oauth2/callback as an allowed redirect URI.

# The friendly domain you (or your organization) have pointed at this
# stack's ALB — DNS is explicitly out of scope for this stack (see
# README's "Hosting the Web UI"), so this must be a domain you manage
# yourself, already pointed (e.g. via CNAME/A record) at the ALB's DNS
# name (available from the AlbDnsName stack output after the first
# deploy). This exact hostname is used to build the OIDC redirect_uri —
# it must match both the DNS record you've created and the redirect URI
# registered on the Okta app below, or login fails with a redirect_uri
# mismatch error from Okta.
WEB_HOSTNAME=travel-agent.example.com

# ARN of an existing ACM certificate for the ALB's HTTPS listener. Must
# already be issued and validated in the same region as the deployment
# (us-east-1) and must cover WEB_HOSTNAME above. This project does not
# provision or import a certificate for you.
WEB_CERTIFICATE_ARN=arn:aws:acm:us-east-1:123456789012:certificate/xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx

# Okta OIDC app endpoints and credentials for web/server.py's own OIDC
# flow. Find these in your Okta org's /.well-known/openid-configuration
# document for the authorization server this app is registered under.
# The client secret is stored in a Secrets Manager secret this stack
# provisions (OidcClientSecret) — it is never passed to the container as
# a plain environment variable.
WEB_OIDC_ISSUER=https://your-org.okta.com/oauth2/default
WEB_OIDC_AUTHORIZATION_ENDPOINT=https://your-org.okta.com/oauth2/default/v1/authorize
WEB_OIDC_TOKEN_ENDPOINT=https://your-org.okta.com/oauth2/default/v1/token
WEB_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=0oaXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
WEB_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret-here
